# Lupus Alpha v0.1

**Status:** Prototype for hypothesis testing  
**Goal:** Verify that LLM (1.5B-7B) writes more accurate code in Lupus than in Python  
**Limitations:** Only minimal language subset (no types, no async, no FFI)

## What works

- [x] Variables (`define`)
- [x] Functions (`define (fn ...)`)
- [x] Arithmetic (`+`, `-`, `*`, `/` — int only)
- [x] Conditional operator (`if`)
- [x] Loops (`while`)
- [x] Lists (`list`, `nth`, `length`)
- [x] Input/Output (`print`)

## What does NOT work (temporarily)

- ❌ Static typing (everything is dynamic)
- ❌ Modules (`senko`, `texas`, `kaltsit`)
- ❌ Asynchronous (`async/spawn`, channels)
- ❌ `match`, `if-let`, `cond`
- ❌ `Option`, `Result`
- ❌ FFI (calling Python from Lupus)
- ❌ Built-in tests (`test`)

## How to run

```bash
python lupus_proto.py examples/calc.lupus
